\chapter{STME-RS-A Test Harness Specification}

\section{Purpose}

This test harness defines subsystem-level validation criteria, failure
envelopes, and stress-test procedures for the STME-RS-A propulsion system.

\section{Subsystem Failure Envelopes}

\subsection{Combustion Chamber Liner}

\begin{itemize}
\item Material: Ta$_4$HfC$_5$ + CNT Matrix
\item Thermal Failure Threshold: 4200 K
\item Mechanical Failure Threshold: 1150 MPa
\item Validation Criterion: No micro-fractures under 3900 K and 820 MPa.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{HTS Magnetic Confinement Coils}

\begin{itemize}
\item Material: REBCO Tape
\item Magnetic Failure Threshold: 15 T
\item Cryogenic Margin: 4.2 K
\item Validation Criterion: No quench events at 14.1 T.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{PZT Acoustic Dampening Array}

\begin{itemize}
\item Material: PZT Ceramics
\item Frequency Limit: 50 kHz
\item Validation Criterion: 40 dB attenuation at 34 kHz oscillation.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Topological Invariant Detector Grid}

\begin{itemize}
\item Invariant: $\mathcal{W}$
\item Drift Threshold: $\Delta \mathcal{W}_{\text{crit}} = 0.15$
\item Validation Criterion: $\Delta \mathcal{W} < 0.03$ under full load.
\end{itemize}

\section{Test Harness Execution Sequence}

\begin{enumerate}
\item Initialize sensor array and telemetry streamer.
\item Ramp magnetic confinement field to 12.4 T.
\item Inject thermal load to 3900 K.
\item Apply overpressure factor of 1.40.
\item Measure:
    \begin{itemize}
    \item residual norms,
    \item geometry–plasma coupling coefficient $\Gamma$,
    \item topological drift $\Delta \mathcal{W}$.
    \end{itemize}
\item Validate against subsystem envelopes.
\item Trigger emergency shutdown if any threshold is exceeded.
\end{enumerate}

\section{Pass/Fail Criteria}

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{PASS:} All subsystems remain within thermal, magnetic,
mechanical, and topological limits.
\item \textbf{FAIL:} Any subsystem exceeds its envelope or drift threshold.
\end{itemize}

\section{Summary}

This test harness provides a deterministic, reproducible validation
framework for certifying STME-RS-A hardware and software subsystems under
extreme operational conditions.